-3. Compute the conjugate $q^* = (w, -x, -y, -z)$ [S3, unofficial].
-4. Compute $v'_{q} = q \otimes v_q \otimes q^*$ using quaternion multiplication [S3, unofficial].
-5. Return the vector part $(v'_x, v'_y, v'_z)$ of the result [S3, unofficial].
